+# Proposal
+
+## Why
+
+Flask's default Jinja autoescape selector only recognizes lowercase template
+extensions. Templates named with uppercase or mixed-case variants of supported
+extensions can therefore render unescaped content unexpectedly.
+
+## What Changes
+
+- Recognize Flask's standard autoescaped template extensions without regard to
+  filename case.
+- Add coverage for uppercase and mixed-case supported extensions while retaining
+  the existing behavior for unsupported filenames and `None`.
+
+## Capabilities
+
+### New Capabilities
+
+- `jinja-autoescape-selection`: Select default Jinja autoescaping from a
+  template filename, including case-insensitive standard extensions.
+
+### Modified Capabilities
+
+- None.
+
+## Impact
+
+- `src/flask/sansio/app.py` default autoescape selection.
+- Templating tests covering `Flask.select_jinja_autoescape`.
