+# Spec Delta
+
+## Purpose
+
+Defines how Flask chooses default Jinja autoescaping from a template filename.
+
+## ADDED Requirements
+
+### Requirement: Case-insensitive supported template extensions
+Flask SHALL enable default Jinja autoescaping when a template filename ends in
+one of the standard supported extensions (`.html`, `.htm`, `.xml`, `.xhtml`,
+or `.svg`), regardless of the extension's letter case.
+
+#### Scenario: Uppercase supported extension
+- **WHEN** a template filename ends in `.HTML`
+- **THEN** default Jinja autoescaping is enabled
+
+#### Scenario: Mixed-case supported extension
+- **WHEN** a template filename ends in `.SvG`
+- **THEN** default Jinja autoescaping is enabled
+
+#### Scenario: Unsupported extension
+- **WHEN** a template filename has no supported extension
+- **THEN** default Jinja autoescaping remains disabled
+
+#### Scenario: Missing template filename
+- **WHEN** no template filename is provided
+- **THEN** default Jinja autoescaping remains enabled
